Some extensions may be restricted to particular architectures; this is
documented in the list of extensions below.

@cindex @code{-march=} command line option, CSKY
@item -march=@var{architecture}
This option specifies the target architecture.  The assembler will issue
an error message if an attempt is made to assemble an instruction which
will not execute on the target architecture.  The following architecture
names are recognized:
@code{ck510},
@code{ck610},
@code{ck801},
@code{ck802},
@code{ck803},
@code{ck804},
@code{ck805},
@code{ck807},
@code{ck810},
and
@code{ck860},
If both @code{-mcpu} and
@code{-march} are specified, the assembler will use
the setting for @code{-mcpu}.

The architecture option can be extended with the same instruction set
extension options as the @code{-mcpu} option.

@cindex @code{-EB} command line option, CSKY
@cindex @code{-mbig-endian} command line option, CSKY
@item -EB
@item -mbig-endian
This option specifies that the output generated by the assembler should
be marked as being encoded for a big-endian processor.

@cindex @code{-EL} command line option, CSKY
@cindex @code{-mlittle-endian} command line option, CSKY
@item -EL
@item -mlittle-endian
This option specifies that the output generated by the assembler should
be marked as being encoded for a little-endian processor.

Note: The assembler will mark the output as a little-endian object by default.

@cindex @code{-pic} command line option, CSKY
@cindex @code{-fpic} command line option, CSKY
@item -pic
@item -fpic
This option specifies that jump instrucitons will genarate dynamic relocations.

@cindex @code{-m@{no-@}ljump} command line option, CSKY
@item -m@{no-@}ljump
This option indicates that some directives will be translated to 'jmpi' or not.

Default: disable

@cindex @code{-m@{no-@}force2bsr} command line option, CSKY
@item -m@{no-@}force2bsr
This option indicates that 'jbsr' will be translated to 'bsr' or not.

Default: disable

@cindex @code{-m@{no-@}jsri2bsr} command line option, CSKY
@item -m@{no-@}jsri2bsr
This option indicates that 'jsri' will be translated to 'bsr' or not.

Default: disable

@cindex @code{-mnolrw} command line option, CSKY
@item -mnolrw
This option indicates that 'lrw' will be translated to 'movi/movih' or not.

Default: disable

@cindex @code{-m@{no-@}literals-after-func} command line option, CSKY
@item -m@{no-@}literals-after-func
@item -m@{no-@}laf
This option indicates that enable dump literals after every function or not.

Default: disable

@cindex @code{-m@{no-@}anchor} command line option, CSKY
@item -m@{no-@}anchor
This option indicates that 'lrw' will be translated to addi rtb/rdb + offset or not.

Default: disable

@cindex @code{-m@{no-@}elrw} command line option, CSKY
@item -m@{no-@}elrw
This option indicates that 'lrw' will be translated to addi rtb/rdb + offset or not.

Default: disable

@cindex @code{-m@{no-@}literals-after-br} command line option, CSKY
@item -m@{no-@}literals-after-br
@item -m@{no-@}labr
This option indicates that the assembler dump literals after every br instruction or not.

Default: enable

@cindex @code{-m@{no-@}istack} command line option, CSKY
@item -m@{no-@}istack
This option indicates that using nie/nir/ipop/ipush intructions in the interrupt services.

Default: Enable in CK801/CK802/CK803 architecture, and others disable.

@cindex @code{-mcallgraph} command line option, CSKY
@item -mcallgraph
This option indicates that the assembler genarates callgraph file which records
functions-call-stack-depths.

Default: disable

@cindex @code{-m@{no-@}callgraph} command line option, CSKY
@item -m@{no-@}callgraph
This option indicates that reserve function call related relocs or not.

Default: enable

@cindex @code{-m@{no-@}callgraph-reloc} command line option, CSKY
@item -m@{no-@}callgraph-reloc
This option indicates that emit callgraph reloc information or not.

Default: diable

@cindex @code{-mmp} command line option, CSKY
@item -mmp
This option indicates that support multiple processor instructions set.
It will be contained by @code{-mcpu=} option normally.

Default: not support.

@cindex @code{-mcp} command line option, CSKY
@item -mcp
This option indicates that support corprocessor instructions set.
It will be contained by @code{-mcpu=} option normally.

Default: not support.

@cindex @code{-mdsp} command line option, CSKY
@item -mdsp
This option indicates that support DSP instructions set.
It will be contained by @code{-mcpu=} option normally.

Default: not support.

@cindex @code{-mcache} command line option, CSKY
@item -mcache
This option indicates that support cache prefetch instructions set.
It will be contained by @code{-mcpu=} option normally.

Default: not support.

@cindex @code{-msecurity} command line option, CSKY
@item -msecurity
This option indicates that support security instructions set.
It will be contained by @code{-mcpu=} option normally.

Default: not support.

@cindex @code{-mhard-float} command line option, CSKY
@item -mhard-float
This option indicates that support hard-flaot instructions set.
It will be contained by @code{-mcpu=} option normally.

Default: not support.

@cindex @code{-mtrust} command line option, CSKY
@item -mtrust
This option indicates that support trust instructions set.
It will be contained by @code{-mcpu=} option normally.

Default: not support.

@cindex @code{-medsp} command line option, CSKY
@item -medsp
This option indicates that support enhance-DSP instructions set.
It will be contained by @code{-mcpu=} option normally.

Default: not support.

@cindex @code{-mvdsp} command line option, CSKY
@item -mvdsp
This option indicates that support vector-DSP instructions set.
It will be contained by @code{-mcpu=} option normally.

Default: not support.

@end table


